I added `outstanding(boatId)` to `BookingBook`, placed just before `forBoat`. It goes over the book's bookings for that boat in the "held" or "confirmed" state and sums `chargePence - paidPence`, counting only positive amounts, so overpaid bookings add nothing. An unknown boat or no matching bookings gives 0, and nothing in the book is changed.

I couldn't see the file body, so I anchored the edit on the `forBoat(boatId: string): Booking[] {` line from the outline, assuming it appears exactly once and the class uses 2-space indentation. I read `this.bookings` directly rather than calling `forBoat`, since I didn't know whether `forBoat` filters by state.
